================================================================
Date: 2026-11-13 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)
Repo: PTPMHDV_Frontend, branch: nguyen
OS: Microsoft Windows 11 Home Single Language (NT 10.0.26200.0)
Node: v24.21.0
npm: 11.19.0
Code SHA (HEAD at test time): bd90b2d5cebd3727b81b26c6244558aa4e53e601
Base SHA (merge-base with origin/main): 02a44baa2dcaa5b916e0168f344625059b146749
Backend reference: origin/main 0b78fb5 (read-only; no Backend file was changed)

Scope of change
---------------
- packages/api-contract/openapi.yaml fully rewritten as one consolidated contract
  for the Web client. Every path item was read from the real Express routers on
  Backend origin/main and cross-checked against the Gateway mount table in
  gateway/src/app.ts. No API behaviour was changed and no Backend file was
  touched.
- Paths: 87 real route keys (no /api prefix) covering auth, QR login, PIN, users,
  KYC, merchants/outlets/API keys, wallets (incl. admin + reconciliation),
  payments (incl. P2P, top-ups, VNPAY), funding (cash-out + VNPAY), utilities,
  notifications, and admin (dashboard, KYC, merchants, audit logs, reconciliation).
- The same 87 path items are repeated under /api/... at the end of `paths`
  because Prism serves path keys directly and does not prepend servers[].url.
  These are generated $ref aliases, not new routes; a script verified a 1:1
  mapping in both directions.
- openapi 3.0.3 (matches the service docs and the Prism setup), servers: [/api],
  global security [bearerAuth], and `security: []` on the public routes
  (signup/signin/refresh/signout, QR init/status, VNPAY IPN/return).
- components: 18 parameters, 7 shared responses, 53 schemas, plus
  `x-contract-sources` mapping each service to its route files and mounts.
- `x-planned-paths` is intentionally EMPTY: no route the Web client calls is
  missing from Backend origin/main. A comment in the file explains the rule and
  points unknown routes to docs/CONTRACT_OPEN_QUESTIONS.md.
- Merchant outlet QR is documented as display-only: "QR diem ban chi hien thi,
  khong co route xac minh tren Web" (full Vietnamese sentence appears in the
  info description and on the outlet-QR operation).
- Topup manual approve/reject are documented as always answering 400 NOT_ALLOWED;
  wallet and reconciliation adjust routes are documented as not accepting
  `Idempotency-Key`.
- docs/CONTRACT_OPEN_QUESTIONS.md rewritten: confirmed shapes per owner and the
  remaining gaps (QR polling secret name, QR status enum, `expiresIn` and
  `remainingLockSeconds` field names, KYC status filter ignored, W2-W4 rollout,
  amount type differences).
- packages/api-contract/README.md updated with the alias rule, the
  x-planned-paths rule and the `npm run contract:lint` command.
- Note: two FE/Backend mismatches found during recon are recorded but were NOT
  fixed here because fixes belong to the auth feature, outside N21 scope:
  (a) auth.api.ts sends `?secret=` while the Backend reads `?pollSecret=` /
  `x-poll-secret`; (b) the FE QR status type lists SCANNED/CONFIRMED/EXPIRED
  while the Backend only returns PENDING/APPROVED/REJECTED (expired = 410).

