Risks / open items
------------------
- QR sign-in is currently broken end-to-end on the Web: the client sends
  `?secret=` while the Backend requires `?pollSecret=`/`x-poll-secret`, and the
  FE status type expects SCANNED/CONFIRMED/EXPIRED values the Backend never
  returns. Both are recorded in docs/CONTRACT_OPEN_QUESTIONS.md; the fix belongs
  to the auth feature and was out of N21 scope.
- Prism enforces the global bearer security, so anyone using `npm run mock` must
  send any `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header for protected paths. This is
  documented in the contract README and in the open-questions doc.
- The 193 redocly warnings are operationId/tag noise from the minimal ruleset
  plus the intentional /api aliases. Adding operationIds to both the real paths
  and the aliases would create duplicate-operationId noise instead, so it was
  left as-is; the exit code is 0.
- Admin reconciliation reports/anomalies (W2-W4) depend on the wallet-service
  rollout; the contract encodes them but live behaviour is still unverified.
- Local Backend `nguyen` is behind origin/main; all shapes were read via
  `git show origin/main:<path>`. No pull, merge, push or PR was performed.
- The branch is local only; nothing was pushed.
